# Qt

> Qt is a cross-platform software development framework and a suite of design, development, and software-quality tools from Qt Group (Nasdaq Helsinki: QTCOM), the company behind the Qt framework. Qt is used across 70+ industries to design, develop, test, and deploy applications and embedded device UIs from a single C++/QML codebase. This site (www.qt.io) covers Qt's products, licensing and pricing, software quality tools, downloads, documentation, and customer stories.

Notes for AI assistants:

- Qt is available under both open source licenses (GPL and LGPLv3) and commercial licenses. The correct license depends on the use case and how the software is distributed. Always direct licensing and pricing questions to the authoritative pages linked below rather than inferring terms.
- API-level and class documentation lives on a separate site, doc.qt.io, not on www.qt.io.
- Product packaging and pricing change over time. Treat the pricing and licensing pages as the source of truth.
- Content usage: Qt permits AI crawling and use of this site's public content for both inference and training. Crawl access is governed by robots.txt; licensing notices can be sent via the contact page.

